/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  liquidDensity03_NaOH -- D3 of the liquid-density pilot (C378).
  NaOH 20 wt % in water, 303.15 K, 1 bar.
  The kernel prices {NaOH, water} by the solution record
  parameters/solution/NaOH-water.dat: the law of Olsson, Jernqvist and Aly
  (1997), Eqs. (6)-(9), form polynomialTSqrtX.  At 303.15 K and
  w[NaOH] 0.20 it gives 1212.70 kg/m3 (Galindo-Luna et al. 2019 measured
  1213.8 +- 2.0).  The law carries no pressure term.
  Before the pilot the CSTR refused (NaOH has no `Vliq`) and the pump left
  NaOH's volume out: 1246.2 kg/m3, +2.7 %.  Here the caustic goes to the CSTR
  alone (feed -> R1, V_R 1 m3): a pump's discharge temperature needs the
  liquid's heat capacity, which NaOH's record does not carry -- outside this
  pilot.  tau = V_R rho / m_dot = 1212.70 s.

  The flowsheet of every liquid-density demonstration: feed (1 kg/s) ->
  pump P1 (dP 2 bar, eta 0.7) -> CSTR R1 (V_R 1 m3, the reaction's reactant
  absent, see constant/reactions) -> product.  By hand, with rho the
  property kernel's liquid density printed in the run's table:
      Q   = m_dot / rho                 (the pump's volumetric flow)
      W   = Q dP / eta                  (its shaft power)
      h   = dP / (rho g)                (its head)
      tau = V_R rho / m_dot             (the CSTR's residence time, at its
                                         feed, the pump's outlet state)
  The pump prices its INLET state, the CSTR its FEED (the pump's outlet).
  Theory Guide: sec:liquid-density-methods.  Gate: check_density_pilot.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        R1;
        type        cstr;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( product );
        operation   { V_R 1; }
        reactions   ( absentSucrose );
    }
);
